// ---------- Layer 3: reference ----------

= Folder structure

`{dataset}` and `{topic}` are placeholders: e.g. `occupation_clean.R`,
`occupation_analyse_wages.R`. The `mtcars_*` files in the template are demos.

#v(0.2cm)
// The tree is drawn without kind badges (edit/run/generated...): every entry is
// passed as kind "dir", which gives no badge and one plain colour.
#let plain-tree(root, entries) = fc-tree(root, entries.map(e => {
  let e = e
  e.insert("kind", "dir")
  e
}))

#plain-tree("better_projects_template/", (
  (name: "data/", kind: "dir", note: [All data. Contents git-ignored; `.gitkeep` keeps the empty folders.]),
  (name: "raw/", depth: 1, kind: "ext", note: [Original data as received. *Never modified.* Often too sensitive or large for GitHub.]),
  (name: "clean/", depth: 1, kind: "gen", note: [One `.rds` per dataset, written by its clean script.]),
  (name: "misc/", depth: 1, kind: "src", note: [`workbook.xlsx`: hand-edited Excel file, one sheet per thing. R only reads it.]),
  (name: "scripts/", kind: "dir", note: [All code. Always committed.]),
  (name: "functions.R", depth: 1, kind: "src", note: [Project functions (`f_` prefix). Every script sources it at the top.]),
  (name: "{dataset}_clean.R", depth: 1, kind: "run", note: [One per dataset. Raw → `data/clean/`. Nothing downstream.]),
  (name: "{dataset}_analyse_{topic}.R", depth: 1, kind: "run", note: [One or more per dataset. `data/clean/` → `output/`.]),
  (name: "main.R", depth: 1, note: [Currently a one-file mtcars/tinytrail demo. Its role is *undecided*.]),
  (name: "output/", kind: "dir", note: [Everything R produces for the report. Contents git-ignored.]),
  (name: "plots/", depth: 1, kind: "gen", note: [PNG/SVG from `ggsave()`.]),
  (name: "tables/", depth: 1, kind: "gen", note: [Typst snippets or CSV, included in `main.typ`.]),
  (name: "data.json", depth: 1, kind: "gen", note: [Inline numbers, read with `json()`.]),
  (name: "typst/", kind: "dir", note: [The document. Typst reads `output/`, never writes to it.]),
  (name: "main.typ", depth: 1, kind: "src", note: [The text. Path variables (`plots`, `tables`, `data`) at the top.]),
  (name: "main.pdf", depth: 1, kind: "out", note: [The finished report.]),
  (name: "template_docs/", kind: "dir", note: [How to use the template.]),
  (name: "Template manual.md", depth: 1, kind: "src", note: [Conventions, how to run, adding a dataset.]),
  (name: "How to write a function.md", depth: 1, kind: "src", note: [Style guide for `functions.R`.]),
  (name: "template_overview.pdf", depth: 1, kind: "out", note: [This document (source `.typ` + `flowlib.typ`).]),
  (name: "99_working_notes/", kind: "dir", note: [Notes about the actual project, not the template.]),
  (name: "daily_log.md", depth: 1, kind: "src", note: [What you did, found and decided. Newest entry on top.]),
  (name: "_tinytrail.yaml", kind: "gen", note: [Provenance log, updated by `tinytrail()`.]),
  (name: ".gitignore", kind: "src", note: [Keeps data and generated files out of git.]),
))

#v(0.3cm)
*In git:* scripts, `typst/main.typ`, `template_docs/` and folder skeletons. *Not in git:* everything in
`data/`, everything R generates, `_tinytrail.yaml` and all PDFs. A collaborator clones the
repo and re-runs the scripts to regenerate the rest. How to run them, naming conventions
and adding a new dataset: see `template_docs/Template manual.md`.

#v(0.3cm)
#fc-box([Good to know], [
  - *Generated files are overwritten* on every run: `data/clean/`, `output/plots/`,
    `output/tables/`, `output/data.json`. Change the script, never the output.
  - *`data.json` is shared* by all analysis scripts. Each merges in its own numbers
    under its dataset's key (see the manual).
  - *Open the project folder* in Positron or VS Code, so the preview can read `output/`.
  - *Order:* clean, analyse, compile. Each script run also updates `_tinytrail.yaml`.
])
